}

data declaration_index_kernel_named_import_escape_note: String = "THE ONE HOLE THE IMPORT-MEMBER ARM DOES NOT CLOSE, HELD OPEN DELIBERATELY AND HELD COUNTABLE. v1.compiler.resolve get_exported_names builds a module's export surface as item names, variant names, the names that module itself LISTS in its own import blocks, and every key of kernel_type_set. The last term means EVERY module in the corpus exports every kernel type name, so the claim import m -- Int -- is admitted whatever m declares. The index mirrors that rather than refusing it, because refusing source the seed compiler accepts is a change to what the seed ACCEPTS, and editing get_exported_names classifies as NewLanguageBehavior, which the v1 freeze refuses and which a refusal dominates every admission of.\n\nMEASURED AGAINST THE INSTALLED COMPILER, not inferred from the code. On a throwaway source root, a module whose entire body is one fn returning Int was imported as import extdeps.probe_missing_anchor -- Int, String, Bool -- and compiled to 6 files with 0 diagnostics. THE ZERO IS READABLE BECAUSE THE NONZERO WAS RUN BESIDE IT: the same source root with a member named probe_absent_member_RED refused with a located MissingExport at the member token, 0 files emitted. So the wall is live and this class walks through it.\n\nTHE SPECIMEN IS NOT SYNTHETIC, and it is a finding in its own right rather than a count. std.types declares no Int, no String and no Float anywhere -- it names them as KEYS of kernel_type_set, which is a different fact -- and modules across the corpus author import std.types -- Int, String. Every one of those claims is false about std.types and always has been. The reason nobody noticed is precisely the escape: the claim is unfalsifiable, so its frequency is zero by construction, which is the absorbing-fallback shape in its purest form -- a deficit whose frequency is zero because nothing can ever report it, not because it does not occur.\n\nKERNEL-NAMED AND DECLARED ARE INDEPENDENT AXES, AND THE SPLIT IS THE FINDING. Measured over dag/std/types.dag against the eight keys of kernel_type_set: FIVE are genuinely declared there -- Bool, Secret, Json, Unit, Bytes -- and THREE are not -- Int, String, Float. So import std.types -- Bool is a TRUE claim and import std.types -- Int is a FALSE one, and a counter that renders them identically would be reporting that a name appears in kernel_type_set, which needs no census to learn. import_member_is_kernel_named splits them by ORDER: it asks import_surface_has FIRST and consults the kernel set only when the target really declares nothing. An ordering is an implementation detail until something asserts the behaviour it produces, so kernel_named_counter_splits_declared_from_undeclared plants both arms under one member name -- a module that declares it and one that does not -- and requires the counter to answer 1 rather than 2. Reversing the two conjuncts leaves every other arm green and reds that one. The COUNT over the live corpus is not transcribed here: it is emitted as import_members_kernel_named on every required run, and a number copied into prose is the positional citation DESIGN section 3 forbids.\n\nWHAT THIS CHANGE DOES ABOUT IT, which is the only thing DESIGN section 5 permits an arm that widens to do: make the frequency OBSERVABLE. A bare continue would have zeroed the deficit exactly as the corpus does, so the class could never rank for repair -- section 6 prices by displaced cost and a masked cost displaces nothing. It is now counted as import_members_kernel_named on DeclarationIndexPopulation and printed beside every other denominator in both the required-ci and the standalone sweep lines, so a green names it. It is NOT reported as a finding and does not stop the line.\n\nTHE EVIDENCE IS AT THE FIXTURE BOUNDARY, where DESIGN section 4b requires it and where the corpus cannot reach: kernel_named_import_member_is_admitted_but_counted plants the claim and requires BOTH no finding AND a count of exactly one, and a_declared_member_does_not_count_as_kernel_named requires a real member to leave the counter at zero. The first assertion alone would be satisfied by re-silencing the escape; the pair is what makes that a RED.\n\nNEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: get_exported_names grounds its export surface in DEFINITIONS rather than appending the kernel set to every module, at which point import_member_is_kernel_named deletes and the members it admits become ordinary ImportMemberAbsent findings. That is a v1 language-behavior change and is out of scope here; this row is what keeps it ranked."

data declaration_index_authorship_arm_is_not_a_mandatory_tag_region_note: String = "WHY THE LENS AUTHORSHIP ARM IS HOST-SIDE RATHER THAN A SECOND MandatoryTagRegion, recorded because it is the first thing a reviewer will propose and because the reason is a measurement rather than a preference.\n\nv2.lens.mandatory_tag already models exactly this shape: a MandatoryTagRegion names a dotted prefix, a required declaration name and a required type name, and mandatory_tag_law states that a violating module FAILS COMPILATION with a typed, located diagnostic -- unwritable at definition admission, not flagged post-hoc by a corpus scan. mandatory_tag_lens is enrolled in v2.compiler.00_compile always_required_root_lenses. So the obvious move is one more region with prefix v2.lens., required declaration construction_justification, required type ConstructionJustification.\n\nIT DOES NOT FIRE. Measured on the installed compiler: a module declaring itself extdeps.probe_missing_anchor, carrying no extdeps_external_authority_anchor and matched by none of that region's exempt_modules, exempt_module_prefixes or exempt_module_suffixes rows, compiled to 5 files with 0 diagnostics. The v2 compile door is not on the gunbc compile path; the executing compiler is the v1 seed. The zero is readable because the same source root produced a located MissingExport refusal in the control described in the sibling row above, so the compiler does refuse at ingestion -- this gate is simply not reached.\n\nWHAT IS AND IS NOT CLAIMED. This is a note about REACHABILITY of one gate from one path, and it is not a defect finding filed against v2.lens.mandatory_tag, whose fold is correct and whose own witness exercises it. It is the reason the authorship obligation is answered here instead: an arm enrolled in a door that the required run never opens would be green by construction, which DESIGN section 4b calls worse than absent because it gets cited as coverage. When the v2 compile door is the executing ingestion, this arm is the one that should dissolve into a MandatoryTagRegion, and that is its next rung."

data declaration_index_citation_debt_contract_note: String = "THE FOUR CONDITIONS DESIGN SECTION 5 PUTS ON A MONOTONE DEBT CONTRACT, ANSWERED ONE BY ONE, because without all four a one-sided ratchet over hand-authored rows is only a quieter snapshot -- it counts the subjects someone remembered to author.\n\n1. INDEPENDENTLY DISCOVERED AND CLOSED SUBJECT UNIVERSE. The universe is every authored DeclarationRef in a non-fixture module, discovered by this index from the corpus's own parse rather than enrolled by anyone. It is CLOSED because membership is decided by the same walk that decides the wall: a citation is in the universe if a swept module's source contains it, and there is no route by which a citation exists and the universe does not contain it. This is the condition the mechanism this change replaces FAILED -- v2.lens.cited_symbol_resolution's population was five hand-listed carriers, so a carrier nobody enrolled was outside the universe by default, and the census could not see DESIGN's own worked example.\n\n2. IDENTITY GRAIN, NOT COUNT. A row is the triple of cited module path, cited declaration name and cited field. Nothing anywhere compares a total. One row being replaced by a duplicate of another is not a state this contract can occupy, because the rows are a set of identities and the check is membership.\n\n3. ROADMAP-JUSTIFIED DIRECTION. The direction is toward zero authored citations that name nothing, which is the executing half of DESIGN section 3's cite-the-symbol-not-the-position rule; the lane that owns it is the one this carrier already names, v1-hand-queue-drain. The roster's terminal state is empty, at which point PRE_EXISTING_CITATION_DEBT and citation_debt_findings both delete.\n\n4. TYPED DISPOSITION ON EVERY REMOVAL, and this is the one worth spelling out because two edits that look identical in a diff must not be the same act. A row leaves this roster in exactly one way: the citation it names stops refusing, because someone repaired it. Both other directions are REFUSED, in opposite arms, which is what makes this a contract rather than a suppression list. Delete a row while its citation still refuses and the citation becomes an ordinary CitedDeclarationAbsent finding and stops the line -- so a row cannot be dropped to buy a green. Repair a citation and LEAVE its row standing and citation_debt_findings emits CitationDebtRowStale naming the spent row -- so the roster cannot rot into a list of things that used to be true. The two arms close the loop in both directions, and neither is a judgement call: each is decided by re-running the same resolution the wall runs.\n\nWHAT IS NOT CLAIMED. The rows are not repaired here, and that is a scope decision rather than a coverage claim: the repair for a citation is a judgement about what its author MEANT, across 38 distinct targets with 38 owners, and guessing it is how a stale citation becomes a confidently wrong one."

data declaration_index_false_quantifier_residue_note: String = "DECLARED RESIDUE: THIS WALL CLOSES THE STALE-SYMBOL HALF AND LEAVES THE FALSE-QUANTIFIER HALF ENTIRELY OPEN. Named here so the next reader finds the gap rather than assuming the citation wall covers it.\n\nWHAT THE WALL CHECKS: that a named symbol RESOLVES. What it does not check: that a QUANTIFIED CLAIM ABOUT A POPULATION is true. The two are independent, and the distinction is not hypothetical -- it was measured twice on this branch, both times inside typed carriers, both times a claim about a population that nobody had counted.\n\nSPECIMEN ONE, in the debt roster's own doc comment: FOUR ROWS AT THE END ARE NOT DEBT ... the deleted census's planted controls. The rows were never added, only described, and the wall's first corpus run reported all four controls as ordinary refusals -- so prose describing rows that do not exist produced a real, imminent, wrong red.\n\nSPECIMEN TWO, in this very carrier, authored by the same hand that built the wall: decl_facts is no longer consulted by any required check. False. decl_facts has live .dag consumers and several are floor-discovered witness modules, so that corpus walk still executes inside the required floor.\n\nWHY THE WALL CANNOT REACH EITHER OF THEM, and this is the structural point rather than an omission: decl_facts is a REAL SYMBOL that RESOLVES. The sentence claiming nothing consults it would pass a cited-symbol census cleanly, because every name in it is true and only the QUANTIFIER is false. A resolver answers does this name exist; nothing in this construction answers is this count right. Section 4c states the general form -- prose is unfalsifiable by construction, which is exactly why an invariant, receipt, count or dissolution condition belongs in a typed carrier and not in a sentence.\n\nHOW THEY WERE ACTUALLY CAUGHT, stated because it is the honest rung: by running the wall over the corpus, and by re-reading the carrier against the request before merge. The first is a mechanism; the second is review diligence, which DESIGN calls strictly weaker in exactly the way it calls the deleted inert-lens census's replacement weaker. So this class sits at MITIGATABLE and nothing here climbs it.\n\nNEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a quantified claim in a carrier is DERIVED rather than AUTHORED -- the count is a projection of the population it describes, so the sentence cannot disagree with the corpus because it is not a sentence. Until that lands, a prose quantifier inside a typed carrier is debt, and the two specimens above are its measured instances rather than its bound."
